    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476">

                <pb facs="0559" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.01/160: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-06T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 6,
                                1919, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3686. For Polk.</p>
                <p>Your 4796, October 24, 11 a.m.</p>
                <p>In spite of recent untoward events in Siberia, consideration is still being given
                    to the possibility of recognizing Kolchak in case he survives the present
                    crisis.</p>
                <p>I shall keep you currently informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
